sxml-xsd-test list - List tests with their documents, expected outcomes and applicability

Usage: sxml-xsd-test list [--catalog=FILE] [--test-set=NAME] [TEST-LIST]

Reads the XSD test suite's suite.xml and test sets with sxml's XML
parser and writes each selected test: whether it is a schema test
or an instance test, its documents, the schema documents an
instance test is validated against, the version attributes of
its test set, test group and test, its status, its expected
outcomes, and, when it does not apply to an XSD 1.1 processor,
"skip:" and the reason. The last line counts the tests, those
that apply, and those in scope. The selection is the tests of
TEST-LIST, those of the test set --test-set names, or with neither
every test of the suite. Exits 1 when a test set or test does not
exist or a test is malformed, 3 when a file cannot be read.

Options:
  -h, --help           Show this help and exit
      --catalog=FILE   The suite.xml of the suite (default: third_party/xsdtests/suite.xml)
      --test-set=NAME  Select every test of one test set, such as saxon-Assert

Arguments:
  TEST-LIST  File naming tests, one '<test-set> <group>/<test>' per line

Examples:
  sxml-xsd-test list tests/xsd/slice.txt
  sxml-xsd-test list --test-set=saxon-Assert
